   "title": "Agent ws HTTP-fallback events by result (#1848)",
   "description": "sum by (result) (rate(ws_fallback_total[5m])) \u2014 how often the agent crossed the transport boundary. result=to_http: the socket was down past ws_fallback_after and the main agent resumed HTTP polling; result=back_to_ws: the socket re-established and the agent returned to the ws path. A high to_http rate without matching back_to_ws means the fleet is stuck on HTTP \u2014 do NOT arm any poll-deprecation (design \u00a73.1/\u00a73.2).",
   "type": "timeseries",
